extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 18: Mystic Russia pp.64-66, read from the text layer. IMPORTED UNDER D4, and it is the entry D4''s reasoning turns on: the book tags it Non-Player Character and its Player Note permits it CONDITIONALLY, which is why the heading sweep and the Player Note disagree here in the opposite direction from the Rusalka. NO xp_table, per D3. ''ALL LEVEL ONE AND TWO WATER ELEMENTAL SPELLS'' IS ENUMERATED RATHER THAN GATED, the same decision the Polevoi''s Earth grant takes: spell_traditions_allowed governs a LEVEL-GATED pick and this is an outright grant, so the twenty level-one and level-two Water rows were read off production and named. The five additional spells the book lists all resolve ONLY under the Water: prefix - Command Fish, Summon Sharks/Whales, Summon Storm and Drought have no unprefixed rows at all, and Create Water DOES have one at level 6 which is NOT the row meant: the book cites Rifts Conversion Book One printed 78, the Water Warlock section, and Water: Create Water sits at level 4. Taking the bare name there would have granted a general invocation at a different level from the one the entry means. SPEED IS TWO NUMBERS AND ONLY ONE IS STORED: 2D6+6 on dry ground and 2D6+40 swimming, both up 50% at night. The dry figure is in attribute_dice because it is the one that governs ordinary movement, and the swimming figure is a natural ability. The night doubling of M.D.C. is likewise unstored. THE BOOK SEPARATES ''Natural Abilities'' FROM ''R.C.C. Skills'' AND THIS IMPORT KEEPS THAT SEAM: the climb percentages are printed under Natural Abilities and recorded there. The +30% is for SELECTED skills only. The text layer carries this book''s digit cipher: the M.D.C. line prints ''+2D4xlO'' and the S.D.C.-world line ''!D4xlO ... !D6xlO''."
