# Vodianoi

## Lore

The water spirit: an ugly old man in a loincloth or rags, pale white and
bloated, usually covered in slime, with the paws of a wolf for hands and a
shaggy green tangle of beard and hair. It lives in swamps and at the deepest
point of lakes and rivers - never oceans.

It is treacherous and murderous, similar in temperament to the Leshii but
crueller. It targets the Warlords'' soldiers in particular, capsizing boats and
drowning the unsuspecting, and it plays cat-and-mouse games with travellers,
fishermen and sailors on a particular road, bridge or stretch of bank.

It robs its victims and keeps the takings - weapons, magic items, gems and
precious metals, all water damaged - hidden at the bottom of the deepest water
it can find, worth 4D6x10,000 credits.

## Alignment

Any, but the majority are miscreant (40%), diabolic (30%) or anarchist (20%).
**A player character must be one of the rare good or anarchist ones.**

## GM Notes

**This is the narrowest permission of the six, and the condition is part of
it.** The book does not say "playable but unpleasant" - it says the Vodianoi is
*"not suitable as a player character, **unless** it is one of the rare good or
anarchist ones"*, and puts the rate at **one in 500**.

Even a good or selfish one is easily provoked, cocky and quick to fight, with
little understanding of mortals or of the laws of men. What holds it in line is
respect: it respects raw power, magical power and cunning, and can be impressed
by a mage, a hero or a warrior who earns that.

**Fire does double damage to it.** No other imported Woodland Spirit has a
stated vulnerability to an ordinary element.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'vodianoi');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'vodianoi';

